The value is 12.
The digits is an empty list of whole numbers.
Repeat while value is more than 0.
The digit is value modulo 10.
Place digit into digits.
Set value to value divided by 10.

The final is the last position of digits.
The middle is (final plus 1) divided by 2.
For every left from 0 to middle minus 1.
The right is final minus left.
swap item left of digits and item right of digits.

The pivot is -1.
For every spot from 0 to final minus 1.
If item spot of digits is less than item (spot plus 1) of digits, set pivot to spot.

The valid is 0.
If pivot is at least 0, set valid to 1.
If pivot is less than 0, set pivot to 0.
The chosen is pivot plus 1.
For every spot from pivot plus 1 to final.
If item spot of digits is more than item pivot of digits, set chosen to spot.

swap item pivot of digits and item chosen of digits.
The middle is (pivot plus 1 plus final) divided by 2.
For every left from pivot plus 1 to middle.
The right is final minus (left minus pivot minus 1).
If left is less than right, swap item left of digits and item right of digits.

The answer is 0.
For each digit in digits.
Set answer to answer times 10 plus digit.

If valid is 1, show answer, otherwise show -1.
